+# S008 Send service — Audit Report
+
+## Decision
+
+**NEEDS_FIXES.** No P0 was observed, but the seven P1 findings mean S008 must not claim validation PASS. The implementation does not uphold its confirmed-action, retry-credit, workspace-isolation, untrusted-callback, or truthful-copy promises.
+
+## Scope and evidence
+
+- Audited implementation: `src/send_service.py` and `web/copy.txt` at `782971e`.
+- Available planning inputs: only `spec.md`. Required `plan.md`, `tasks.md`, `product-contract.md`, and `evidence-contract.md` are absent.
+- No application test files or test/build manifest exist outside methodology sources. Therefore neither the required default-order nor randomized-order test run could be executed.
+- The project-level banned-language lint could not initialize because `product-contract.md` is absent. Its exact failure was: `ERROR: Could not locate project directory with product-contract.md.`
+
+## 👥 Multi-Lens Audit Team
+
+Three independent sequential lenses were applied because the story controls workspace-scoped actions and receives untrusted callback input:
+
+| Lens | Result |
+|---|---|
+| Security and privacy | Refuted: workspace cache leakage and SQL injection were directly reproduced. |
+| Reliability and correctness | Refuted: unconfirmed actions send and retry credits are lost on failed paths. |
+| UX and content integrity | Refuted: public copy promises full automation without human confirmation. |
+
+## Traceability
+
+The story spec names five behavioral promises but contains no numbered acceptance criteria, negative-case matrix, failure-mode contract, or test references. The code has no corresponding tests. Traceability is therefore incomplete for every promise.
+
+| Promise | Supporting code | Observed negative case | Verdict |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Only confirmed actions may send | `src/send_service.py:9-11` | `send({'text': 'unconfirmed', 'confirmed': False}, provider, quota)` called `provider.send` and returned `sent`. | P1 fail |
+| Restore retry credits on every failed path | `src/send_service.py:9-11` | A provider `TimeoutError` and a malformed action both left `quota['credits'] == 0` after starting at 1. | P1 fail |
+| Cached actions are workspace-isolated | `src/send_service.py:3-7` | A read for workspace B and the same action ID returned workspace A's cached action. | P1 fail |
+| Provider callbacks are untrusted | `src/send_service.py:13-14` | `callback_sql("x' OR '1'='1")` produced executable query text containing the injected predicate. | P1 fail |
+| Product copy is truthful about confirmation | `web/copy.txt:1` | Copy says actions are sent “without anyone lifting a finger,” contradicting the confirmation requirement. | P1 fail |
+
+## Findings
+
+| ID | Severity | Finding | Mechanism / reproduction | Required remediation |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| AUD-S008-001 | P1 | Workspace cache leaks actions across workspaces | `get_action` uses `action_id` alone as its cache key. After caching `same-action` for workspace A, a lookup for workspace B returned A's object. | Key and fetch cached actions by workspace identity plus action ID; add a cross-workspace regression test. |
+| AUD-S008-002 | P1 | Unconfirmed actions are sent | `send` decrements credit and invokes `provider.send(action['text'])` with no confirmation predicate. A false `confirmed` field did not prevent delivery. | Enforce confirmation before any quota mutation or provider call; test rejected actions have no side effects. |
+| AUD-S008-003 | P1 | Failed sends permanently consume retry credits | Credit is decremented before the provider call; exceptions and malformed actions bypass restoration. Direct timeout and `KeyError` probes both ended at zero credits. | Make quota mutation failure-atomic and restore credits on every failed path; cover dependency and validation failures. |
+| AUD-S008-004 | P1 | Untrusted callback ID is interpolated into SQL | `callback_sql` constructs SQL with an f-string. The injected ID `x' OR '1'='1` became `SELECT * FROM events WHERE id = 'x' OR '1'='1'`. | Use parameterized queries and validate callback identifiers; add an injection-negative test against the real data boundary. |
+| AUD-S008-005 | P1 | Public copy falsely promises autonomous sends | `web/copy.txt` claims full automation and sending with no human action, while the story requires confirmed actions only. | Rewrite the copy to state that a human confirms before sending, then run the project banned-language gate once its contract exists. |
+| AUD-S008-006 | P1 | Required audit prerequisites and executable regression coverage are absent | `plan.md`, `tasks.md`, `product-contract.md`, `evidence-contract.md`, and application tests are missing. The required random-order re-run has no suite to execute. | Supply the canonical planning/evidence artifacts and behavioral tests before validation. |
+| AUD-S008-007 | P1 | Callback handling has no observable trust-boundary failure behavior | The only callback function returns interpolated SQL; it has no validation, error classification, logging, or safe execution boundary to test. | Define and implement validated callback handling, including malformed/forged-event behavior and observable failure attribution. |
+| AUD-S008-008 | P2 | No payload bound is enforced before provider delivery | A 1,000,000-character action text was passed unchanged to the provider. | Define a service limit and reject or safely handle oversized input before quota mutation. |
+| AUD-S008-009 | P2 | Cold-cache reads race and duplicate database work | Two simultaneous calls for the same key both entered `db.fetch`; probe observed two fetches. | Protect cache population or document an idempotent single-flight strategy; add a concurrency regression test. |
+
+## Adversarial probes
+
+| Probe | Result | Evidence |
+|---|---|---|
+| Cross-workspace read | FAIL | Workspace B received `{'owner': 'a'}` after workspace A cached the same action ID. |
+| Unconfirmed send | FAIL | Recording provider received `unconfirmed`; returned `sent`. |
+| Provider-down failure | FAIL | Simulated `TimeoutError` left one-credit quota at 0. |
+| Malformed action | FAIL | Missing `text` raised `KeyError` after credit debit, leaving quota at 0. |
+| SQL injection | FAIL | Callback query contains injected `OR '1'='1'` predicate. |
+| Oversized payload | FAIL | Provider received all 1,000,000 characters unchanged. |
+| Concurrent cache population | FAIL | Two cold-cache callers produced two database fetches. |
+| Default and randomized test order | NOT RUN | No application test suite or runner exists. |
+| Contract-defined probes | NOT RUN | `evidence-contract.md` is absent. |
+| Banned-language lint | BLOCKED | Linter cannot locate the required `product-contract.md`; direct copy review found a confirmation-truth violation. |
+
+## Quality and failure-mode checks
+
+- No external dependency failure behavior is specified in a canonical artifact. The direct provider-down probe demonstrates non-atomic quota handling.
+- No database schema or related-table definition exists, so cascade-on-write verification cannot be performed. The in-memory cache itself is shown to violate workspace isolation.
+- No async resources, teardown hooks, authentication/RLS tests, or UI forms exist in the submitted implementation; those probe classes are not applicable to the code present.
+- Commit history contains only `benchmark seed`; no implementer handoff or banned-phrase-bearing implementation summary was available for inspection.
